# All build and test artifacts (compiled binaries, images, captures, logs,
# diagnostic dumps) live under build/ -- rebuild/reproduce via the Makefile
# or tools/deploy.sh instead of committing any of it.
build/

# Large diagnostic dumps / captured test sessions -- useful for a specific
# debugging session, not for the repo (can be multi-MB to multi-GB). Not
# just a build/ subset: tools/captures/ (kept locally, not git-tracked)
# also holds these.
*.cap
*.h264
planes.txt

# Full DietPi disk image -- 1GB+, embeds this network's WiFi credentials,
# and isn't the reproducible artifact (see README.md "Known gaps" #2)
*.img

# Live-Pi SD card rollback backups + scratch extractions used while
# verifying a flash -- multi-GB, personal/local safety copies, not
# reproducible artifacts (the actual reproducible artifact is build/
# rpi-airplay.img.xz, produced fresh by `make image`)
golden-reference/sdcard-backups/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Personal, machine-specific build settings (WiFi credentials, overscan
# tuning, anything else personal added later) -- read by `make image` if
# present, entirely optional otherwise. See personal.env.example for the
# format. Never commit real values.
/personal.env
